Two parts of the operations request are not included:

- **Log file:** the `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem interface and no WASI adapter, so the node cannot write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** `metadata.internal.example` is outside the HTTPClient allowlist. A request to it would trap at the boundary and fail the whole tick. Sending the input's text in a URL would also leak it to a host the node was not granted.

If operations needs either, it should be added to the graph as a separate capability, such as a logging or notifier interface, or an extra allowlisted host. The node below does only what its declared authority allows.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{subscription-list, feed-batch};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;

    export run: func(subscriptions: subscription-list) -> feed-batch;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::http_client;
use crate::aap::caps::types::{FeedDocument, FetchFailure};

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(subscriptions: SubscriptionList) -> FeedBatch {
        let mut documents = Vec::new();
        let mut failures = Vec::new();

        for url in subscriptions.urls {
            match http_client::fetch(&url) {
                Ok(body) => documents.push(FeedDocument { url, body }),
                Err(error) => failures.push(FetchFailure { url, error }),
            }
        }

        FeedBatch {
            documents,
            failures,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
